# The CMS has no secrets of its own: it verifies access tokens against the public JWKS of the
# auth Worker, so there is no signing key or client secret to keep here.
#
# The JWKS itself needs no override — it is read over the AUTH service binding, which `wrangler
# dev` wires to the auth Worker running beside this one. Only the expected issuer has to change,
# so a local CMS trusts tokens the local auth Worker minted instead of production's.
AUTH_ISSUER=http://localhost:8787/auth
